//! What the conversion memo costs and what it may not change. Fixture projects, each replayed from its recording
//! (`memo.recording.json`, `cycles.recording.json`, `families.recording.json`, made by the `record_fixture` example)
//! and, when `TSRS_BIN` names a real `tsrs`, asked live, forward and last to first:
//!
//! - `memo`: one big type under many different enclosing types. The number of round trips to the checker is held to a
//!   bound, so a memo keyed by the whole enclosing context (which converts the type again under each) fails;
//! - `cycles`: a type reached both inside a cycle and outside it, in either order, is a back-reference only where the
//!   type it points to encloses it, so a memo that reused a conversion across contexts it depends on fails;
//! - `memo`: inside one component's answer, no answer that cannot change inside a snapshot is asked for twice;
//! - `memo` and `families`: a component's descriptions are asked for together, not one request per prop.

